---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="BitEvo — Authority Engineering Services for AI Agents" description="A decision ladder for AI-agent workflows: qualify the action chain, test one failure, audit authority and evidence, then harden verified weaknesses.">
  <section class="services-hero section">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Engineering decision ladder</div><h1 class="display">Give the workflow only the authority its evidence can support.</h1></div>
      <div><p class="lede">BitEvo engagements are organized around one progression: identify the critical action, test the uncertainty, decide whether authority should expand or contract, then repair only what verified evidence supports.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/audit-intake">Map a workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-rule">
    <div class="container service-stack">
      <article class="service panel">
        <div class="service-index">01</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Qualification</div><h2>Scope / Authority Triage</h2><p>Identify one external effect, the authority required to create it, the owner of that authority and whether a staging/test path exists. The outcome is a simple decision: audit this workflow or do not.</p><div class="chips"><span>20 minutes</span><span>1 critical action</span><span>owner identified</span><span>qualification only</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>Free</strong><small>20 min</small><a class="button" href="/audit-intake">Start with the action →</a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="service panel">
        <div class="service-index">02</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Narrow uncertainty</div><h2>Entry Audit</h2><p>Use when one suspected failure dominates the decision. We test one critical action chain and one primary hypothesis to determine whether the failure is reproducible and decision-relevant.</p><div class="chips"><span>1 action chain</span><span>1 hypothesis</span><span>bounded reproduction</span><span>finding memo</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>$1,500</strong><small>fixed</small><a class="button" href="/audit-intake">Test the hypothesis →</a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="service primary panel">
        <div class="service-index">03</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">Primary authority decision</div><h2>Agent Authority & Evidence Audit</h2><p>Use when the question is broader than one defect: does this workflow have enough evidence, external confirmation and recovery control for its current or proposed authority?</p><div class="chips"><span>5 working days</span><span>1 staging workflow</span><span>up to 3 integrations</span><span>10–20 scenarios</span><span>1 retest</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>$4,900</strong><small>fixed</small><a class="button button-primary" href="/agent-authority-audit">See the decision model →</a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="service panel">
        <div class="service-index">04</div>
        <div class="service-copy"><div class="eyebrow">After verified findings</div><h2>Hardening & Repair</h2><p>Implementation is scoped only after the evidence identifies the control gap. Work is tied to explicit owner decisions, rollback requirements and retest criteria — not a generic promise to “make the agent safe.”</p><div class="chips"><span>finding-led</span><span>separate scope</span><span>rollback-aware</span><span>retest criteria</span></div></div>
        <div class="service-side"><strong>Quoted</strong><small>separately</small><a class="button" href="/pricing">See scope rules →</a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="container principles-grid">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">What stays invariant</div><h2 class="section-title">The method does not change when the budget changes.</h2></div>
      <div class="principles">
        <article><span>01</span><div><strong>Workflow before model</strong><p>The audit object is the chain that can create an external effect: model, data, permissions, tools, approvals and recovery logic together.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>02</span><div><strong>Evidence before authority</strong><p>A workflow should not gain additional action rights when the evidence required to justify those actions is absent, stale or ambiguous.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>03</span><div><strong>External effect before “success”</strong><p>Internal completion is not proof when another system was supposed to change. The effect must be independently observable.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>04</span><div><strong>Owner decision before remediation</strong><p>A finding is useful only when it supports a bounded decision: expand, constrain, repair or retest. Implementation follows that decision.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="narrow closing">
      <div class="eyebrow">First step</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Do not describe the whole AI stack. Name the action that matters.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Start with one thing the workflow can change in the outside world. From that action we can identify the authority boundary, the evidence needed to justify it and the failure path worth testing.</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/audit-intake">Map the critical action <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .services-hero{padding-top:clamp(78px,10vw,132px)}.hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.12fr .88fr;gap:clamp(42px,8vw,110px);align-items:end}.hero-grid .lede{margin:0 0 24px}.service-stack{display:grid;gap:14px}.service{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr 170px;gap:28px;align-items:center;padding:28px 30px}.service.primary{border-color:rgba(127,208,177,.35)}.service-index{align-self:start;color:#57635f;font:500 .66rem var(--mono)}.service-copy .eyebrow{margin-bottom:8px}.service-copy h2{margin:0 0 9px;font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2.5vw,1.75rem);letter-spacing:-.025em}.service-copy p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);max-width:720px}.chips{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}.chips span{padding:5px 8px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;color:#7c8986;font:500 .58rem var(--mono)}.service-side{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-end}.service-side>strong{font-size:1.65rem;letter-spacing:-.04em}.service-side>small{color:var(--muted);font:500 .62rem var(--mono);margin-bottom:18px}.service-side .button{width:100%}
  .principles-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:clamp(44px,8vw,110px)}.principles{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.principles article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:42px 1fr;gap:20px;padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.principles article>span{color:#57635f;font:500 .64rem var(--mono)}.principles strong{font-size:.9rem}.principles p{margin:5px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}.closing{text-align:center}.closing .section-title{margin-inline:auto}.closing .lede{margin:18px auto 28px}
  @media(max-width:900px){.hero-grid,.principles-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.service{grid-template-columns:40px 1fr}.service-side{grid-column:2;align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:row;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}.service-side>small{margin:0;align-self:center}.service-side .button{width:auto;margin-left:auto}}
  @media(max-width:620px){.service{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding:24px}.service-index{display:none}.service-side{grid-column:auto;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start}.service-side .button{width:100%;margin-left:0}.chips{margin-top:14px}}
</style>